        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodland%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Milwaukee Railroad and later a streetcar line ran through the southern part of Woodland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofwoodlandmn.gov/woodland-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The streetcar depot still stands at Maplewood Road, a relic of early 20th‑century transit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofwoodlandmn.gov/woodland-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Woodland’s early development began with a summer cottage built in the 1870s, later expanded into a hotel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
